Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||09-27-2001||08:57 PM||||When I was told to check my throttle linkages by unscrewing two nuts off the air filter and pull it open, but I noticed that when I pull up the air filter, the whole assembly was all one thing (extends to the back and then to a hose) but there was another hose that is plugged to it from underneath it (under where a cap is), and it wasn't even plugged in firmly.  When I moved the air filter up, the mouth and the flexible hose came apart.  I've wondered if that was a bad thing, or if it has never been firmly connected all this time.  I could bring the air filter back down and get the mouth in the hose.  I could try to get a screw-tightening ring (whatever it's called) and make the hose snug with the hole behind the air filter.  If it has been disconnected all these time how can it affect my car?  Or can I leave it like that and take care of it later?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_2.JPG">  <BR>'84 2m4, 4 speed, 106k miles (157k km)  AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ferrari_cdn||09-27-2001||10:54 PM||||*bump*||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||09-28-2001||12:13 AM||||are you talking about a flexible hose about 2" in dia that goes down to the exhaust? It will be toward the drivers seat toward the end of the snorkel where the thermac control is. If that's what you are talking about, it is sometimes called a heat stove tube or pipe. It is to bring warm air from around the exhaust into the air cleaner assy when the eng is cold. Helps emmisions and warmup, especially in cold weather. I don't think my 84 4cyl has a clamp to hold it on, just a snug fit.<BR>You can get a replacemnet at any autozone. <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ferrari_cdn||09-28-2001||12:20 AM||||Yeah thats the one Im talking about.  It wasn't a snug fit, really.  Comes off really easily if I bring the air filter up.  But I think that if the air filter was in place, I don't think it will come out anyway.  But should I find a way to make it snug anyway?||||reg||7
Z||000004||Cheever3000||09-28-2001||12:41 AM||||Doesn't have to be real tight.  Just as long as it reaches and is in position & stays there.<P>||||reg||1
